-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner toggle at q and Vélu quotients of moduli places
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, and let $N,q$ be nonzero naturals with $q$ prime, $q\nmid N$ and $(Nq)\cdot 1\ne 0$ in $K$. Two global hypotheses on level $Nq$ are assumed: that any two places of the full modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,K\,(Nq)$ (the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions) satisfying `IsModuliPlaceOf` for one moduli point coincide; and that every moduli point of level $Nq$ admits a `ModuliTestDatum` $D$ over some extension field whose generic-fibre curve has exactly $q^2$ points killed by $q$ and on which `reduceHom` is injective on $q$-torsion. Let $\tau$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of that field which, for every nonzero $d\mid N$, interchanges the elements $\mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,d\,(\tilde j)$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,(dq)\,(\tilde j)$, where $\tilde j$ is `jqModC`. Let $E/K$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve, $C\le E(K)$ cyclic of order $Nq$, and $Q\in C$ of additive order $q$; assume the Vélu curve $E.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,q$ has nonzero discriminant and admits an additive map $\varphi$ from $E(K)$ with kernel $\mathbb{Z}Q$ and given by Vélu's coordinate sums off $\mathbb{Z}Q$. Let $C''$ be a cyclic subgroup of order $Nq$ of the quotient containing $\varphi(C)$ and $\varphi$ of all $q$-torsion. Then transporting $\mathrm{moduliPlace}\,K\,(Nq)\,E\,C$ along $\tau$ by `Place.congrEquiv` yields $\mathrm{moduliPlace}\,K\,(Nq)\,(E.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,q)\,C''$.
--
--   This is the moduli interpretation of the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_q$ on $X_0(Nq)$, expressed at the level of places of the full modular function field and realised through Vélu's explicit model of $E/\langle Q\rangle$ with the subgroup generated by the images of $C$ and of the $q$-torsion. It feeds the construction of rational isogenies compatible with the action of automorphisms on moduli places used later in the level-lowering machinery.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_congrEquiv_moduliPlace_eq_moduliPlace_fullKernelQuotient_of_atkinLehner.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ModuliPlace
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_FullKernelQuotient
